.TH FCNTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fcntl \- control a file descriptor with an integer argument
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.B int fcntl(int descriptor, int command, int argument);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Performs a Linux F_* command.  Pass zero when no argument is needed.
Use fcntl_ptr for commands requiring a pointer such as F_GETLK.  Unlike GNU
libc's variadic fcntl, Crunch requires all three arguments.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the command result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fcntl_ptr (3crunch),
.BR fcntl (2)
